<title> Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.5.1: Identifying Linear and Exponential Quantities </item>
  <item> 5.5.2: Exponential Decay  </item>
  <list>
    <item> 5.5.2: Self Check  </item>
    <item> 5.5.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.5.3: Using Graphs to Represent Exponential Decay </item>
  <list>
    <item> 5.5.3: Self Check  </item>
    <item> 5.5.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.5.4: Justifying Exponential Models </item>
  <list>
    <item> 5.5.4: Self Check </item>
    <item> 5.5.4: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.5.5: Writing Equations to Represent Exponential Decay  </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 5.5.6: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<para>None</para>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>If possible, acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology as an option for students
  to select during the lesson.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look
    for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral
    explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link> </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson:</para>
